===Etymology===
From Ancient Greek [[πτερόν#Ancient Greek|πτερόν]] (pterón, “wing”) +[[σαῦρος#Ancient Greek|σαῦρος]] (saûros, “lizard”), literally translating to "wing lizard".

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈtɛɹəˌsɔɹ/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of several [[flying]] [[reptile]]s, of the [[extinct]] [[order]] †{{taxfmt|Pterosauria|order}}, including the [[pterodactyl]]s. {{defdate|from ''c''. 1860}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2020|author=Shona Husk|title=Close to the Truth|publisher=HarperCollins Australia|isbn=9781489298799| passage=Batsquatch, '''pterosaurs''' and the River Man. She had three weeks in Washington State tracking down the local legends. There was nothing ordinary about her job as the biologist on the television show ''Cryptid or Hoax?''}}

